mathew@aquila.fccc.edu (George Mathew) writes:
>I compiled CAP on OSF1 with the native Ethertalk option.
>However, nothing works. I have PACKETFILTER option in the
>kernel & the packet filter device files are all in place.
>However, I get nothing on running 'getzones'. 

CAP support for Digital UNIX FDDI interfaces was added in patch number 197.
Check the README file in your CAP source tree to see what version you have
or run any CAP utility with the -dv option. You also need to have
uncommented the USING_FDDI_NET feature in the m4.features file (and then
run gen.makes, make clean, make programs etc).

CAP patches are available at ftp://munnari.OZ.AU./mac/cap.patches/cap60.patch*
If it still doesn't work, let me know.

 - David.



