values.h is not a standard C language header. The headers that define
type limits are limits.h for integral types and float.h for floating
point types.

>I was surprised to see that the values of
>
>MINFLOAT and MINDOUBLE

The macros you want are called FLT_MIN and DBL_MIN in float.h. values.h is
obsolete and not portable.

>are defined less then the compiler can work with!
